The benchmark: a fixed 148 clips (116 training, 32 test) of the training and test sets (docs/plans/bodies-and-movement.md,
section 3's rule of speed), on which every gate of the movement work runs in minutes: the capture's
import, the export, a short run of the tracker and the phase's check. The whole sets confirm what
the benchmark passes; they decide nothing first. Chosen once by the SHA-256 of each clip's name,
with the hard clips put in: 100STYLE's crouched and hopping styles and its runs, CeTI's every task
and its fast walk (w04), ACCAD's strikes, kicks, runs and its crawling and lying. A clip keeps the
set it has in the split above (a benchmark test clip is a test clip).
